Place the @Beef{500%g} in a large #pot{} with @Water{2%liters}. Bring to a boil.
Skim off the foam. Reduce heat, add @Bay leaves{2%pieces}, and simmer for ~{90%minutes}.
Remove the Beef and cut it into pieces. Return to the #pot{}.
Cook the Beets:

Heat @Vegetable oil{2%tablespoons} in a #skillet{} over medium heat.
Add @Beetroot{2%pieces} (grated) and sauté for ~{5%minutes}.
Stir in @Tomato paste{2%tablespoons} and a splash of broth. Simmer for ~{10%minutes}.
Prepare the Vegetables:

Add @Potatoes{3%pieces} (diced) to the #pot{} with broth. Cook for ~{10%minutes}.
Sauté @Onion{1%piece} (chopped) and @Carrots{1%piece} (grated) in a #skillet{} until softened (~{5%minutes}).
Add the sautéed vegetables to the #pot{}.
Add the Beets and Cabbage:

Stir in the cooked @Beetroot{} and @Cabbage{300%g} (shredded). Simmer for ~{15%minutes}.
Season the Soup:

Add @Garlic{2%cloves} (minced), @Salt{}, and @Ground black pepper{} to taste. Simmer for ~{5%minutes}.
Serve:

Ladle the borscht into bowls. Garnish with @Dill{} and a dollop of @Sour cream{}.
